{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791840417,"nonce":"q9oMPeAl+IowxDQhmKV6rfpNFgo=","message":"Checkpoint 6 completed. Harness/workflow commit bf02bec7c9f3b58aac6293eec8a1024456c7849c; retained-results commit fc8a7c46e9832186fad79ad2369ec12553b82570.\n\nActual CI run passed: https://github.com/rayzor-blade/ash/actions/runs/38309406232. Dispatched bench.yml on codex/tree-fusion-ci with tree_fusion_only=true. The existing build artifact was measured on a fresh runner. Normal benchmark lanes, aggregation and website publication were all skipped. Remote main was not pushed. Both commits are on the separate experiment branch.\n\nControlled opt-in comparison: one release executable per host, identical source/bytecode, fusion off/on, seven alternating AB/BA pairs after one warmup pair. Fresh processes include startup and compilation. Diagnostic accounting (two pairs) is separate from timing and disables TLAB on both variants. Inherited ASH_* knobs are removed. Hash/checksum, counter, transformation and helper IR gates all pass. This same-binary flag comparison intentionally isolates the pass; it is not an old/new compiler comparison containing unrelated changes.\n\nCI, AMD EPYC 9V74 (4 exposed CPUs):\n- Clean median whole-process time: 304.990 -\u003e 223.493 ms.\n- Median paired on/off ratio: 0.74864; descriptive 95% paired bootstrap interval [0.69857, 0.75909].\n- Cumulative managed plus external allocation: 900.0 -\u003e 4.0 MiB in both diagnostic pairs (99.556% reduction).\n- Diagnostic peak RSS: off 661.45/661.22 MiB; on 105.35/102.44 MiB.\n- Diagnostic GC: off one collection (21.1/22.8 ms pauses); on zero.\n- Helper 388: 19 ops, 19 registers, no node allocations; recursive IR verified. Cranelift compilation 2.33/2.13 ms, LLVM 18.96/15.79 ms. LLVM installs at 33.7/29.8 ms, during the instrumented workload.\n- Decode plus preparation: off 0.95/1.03 ms, on 5.73/5.63 ms; these instrumented phase costs are not substituted for clean timing.\n\nNUC, Intel i5-1250P (16 logical CPUs), isolated release source snapshot 038b24b458e5ffb808e87c0463567cc1ba5f2cbf:\n- Clean median whole-process time: 334.171 -\u003e 128.234 ms.\n- Median paired on/off ratio: 0.38105; descriptive 95% paired bootstrap interval [0.37482, 0.38645].\n- Cumulative managed plus external allocation: 900.0 -\u003e 4.0 MiB in both diagnostic pairs.\n- Diagnostic peak RSS: off 318.30/316.31 MiB; on 67.52/66.86 MiB.\n- Diagnostic GC: off four collections (18.7/22.2 ms pauses); on zero.\n- Same scalar helper; Cranelift compilation 1.76/1.81 ms, LLVM 7.14/6.65 ms. LLVM installs at 17.8/20.1 ms during the workload.\n- Existing modified ~/ash checkout preserved. Build in ~/ash-tree-fusion-038b24b4 with two Cargo jobs. Missing LLVM 21 Polly package extracted locally; no system package install. Retained run results-02 reads the source revision verified from the transferred git archive. An earlier attempt with a mistyped revision label was discarded before timing analysis.\n\nEvery executed guest (20 per host, including warmup/diagnostics) reports checksum -104864. Separate AIR inspection intentionally exits before executing the guest and supplies no checksum/timing evidence. Source SHA256 d705a3b8c01dd2dcae7a89e27cf814317df8ba50ccbf3ec6d1ea8bfdcfd669b5; bytecode SHA256 9698cecaf8852fa219acfd3361ea8659543cb7dc5a4033168aa3ff96d01a926d. The delayed depth-16 tree still materializes. CI and NUC compiler source is identical; the intervening commit changes only the harness, workflow and documentation.\n\nRetained: bench/baselines/tree-fusion-2026-10-12.json and linked raw .tar.gz archives. Full samples, commands, binary/input/harness hashes, CPU/kernel/toolchains, load snapshots, compiler-phase/tier logs, RSS, GC, stdout/stderr and helper IR are included. Archives verified against summary and all guest checksums. Six harness evidence tests plus eight existing benchmark gate tests pass; local end-to-end harness and workflow YAML validation passed before dispatch.\n\nScope/uncertainty: allocation counters cover GC-managed plus runtime-tracked external allocation, each rounded to 0.1 MiB (sum +/-0.1 MiB). They do not measure cumulative Rust/LLVM malloc traffic; process RSS is separate. Timing distributions are within-host; CI/NUC CPUs, memory sizes and Rust toolchains differ. Instrumented timing is not used as the clean result, and concurrent phase totals overlap. Helper compilation/IR/allocation evidence is separate; no isolated-helper throughput claim. No arena or counter exclusion was introduced. Fusion remains opt-in; AOT/wasm activation remains unsupported. Next: broader-workload cost/regression gates and bounded default rollout in 082042b.","files":null}]}